{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1795543752,"nonce":"0IKZ9YrPRLTfHtRdf1rn7knYFBo=","target":"97b5e27a87912ef94648c0b20b5494c3335c2fde64713d9f99db00c08c5185a4","message":"In a partitioned coupling (`jno/_coupling`), a transient `jno.fem` problem cannot be the side that sends a flux (the Neumann side): the flux it would send is not defined for a transient form yet. The same limitation is stated in `docs/coupling.md` (\"a transient `jno.fem` side cannot send a flux\").\n\n**Reproduce** Couple a transient `jno.fem` problem with another problem so that the FEM side must deliver the flux: Robin-Robin (`alpha=`), or a Dirichlet-Neumann pair assigned the other way round (the FEM side as the Neumann side). The driver then calls `FEMParticipant.sample` on a flux expression of the transient problem. The steady flux read-back is tested in `tests/test_coupling_participants.py`; there is no transient counterpart.\n\n**Expected** The flux at the interface, as a conservative nodal density, for every step of the window.\n\n**Where** `jno/_coupling/participant.py`, `FEMParticipant.sample`: it reads a flux as the consistent reaction, `problem.eval(total weak terms, u)`, projected on the interface nodes by `iface.project`. On a transient form the reaction needs the `u.t` term of the step that produced `u`; `weak_terms` evaluates the free residual at a single state, so the time-derivative part is missing.\n\n**Workaround** Dirichlet-Neumann gives the flux job to the Neumann side, which is the right assignment when the transient FEM side is the stiffer one (it takes the value and sends no flux). Choose that assignment with `dirichlet=...`.\n\n**Direction** Include the `u.t` term of the step (the mass term applied to the difference of the window's end and start states divided by dt, or the time scheme's own step residual) in the reaction before projecting it. Open: which time schemes need it (theta-schemes, bdf2, others) and whether the window-mean flux used for sub-stepping senders (`tests/test_coupling_transient.py::test_a_substepping_sender_passes_its_window_mean_flux_and_heat_is_conserved`) applies here too.","files":null}]}